{title: Commit your way to the Lord}
{subtitle: Psalms 37:5}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Like grass they [Bb]will soon wither
Fade like the green of new [Gm7]growth
Trust in the Lord and [Eb]do good
[F7sus4]Dwell in the land with [Bb]grace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Make faithfulness your pasture
Delight in [Bbmaj7/A]the Lord a[Gm7]lone
He will give what [Gm7/F]your [Eb]heart asks
[F7sus4]When you walk in his [Bb]ways [Bbmaj7/A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Commit your [F]way to the [Eb]Lord [Bb/D]
[Cm7]Trust in him and he will [Bb]act [F/A]
[Gm]Bring out your [F]righteous[Eb]ness
[Bb/D]Like the [Cm7]light [F7sus4]of [Bb]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Be still before the Lord
Wait patiently [F/A]for [Gm7]him
Do not burn [Gm7/F]with an[Eb]ger
[Fsus4]Over the man who pros[Bb]pers [F/A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Commit your [F]way to the [Eb]Lord [Bb/D]
[Cm7]Trust in him and he will [Bb]act [F/A]
[Gm]Bring out your [F]righteous[Eb]ness
[Bb/D]Like the [Cm7]light [F7sus4]of [Bb]day [F/A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Your justice [F]like the noonday [Eb]sun
[Cm7]Shining clear and [Bb]true [F/A]
[Gm]Let go of [F]anger [Eb]now [Bb/D]
[Cm7]Abandon wrath and [Fsus4]fear
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Commit your [F]way to the [Eb]Lord [Bb/D]
[Cm7]Trust in him and he will [Bb]act [F/A]
[Gm]Bring out your [F]righteous[Eb]ness
[Bb/D]Like the [Cm7]light [F]of [Bb]day [F/A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]It leads only [F]to e[Eb]vil
[Cm7]So trust in him a[Bb]lone
{end_of_verse}

